Expected crash: Heap-double-free in wmem_simple_free_all() triggered when Wireshark's RTPS dissector (packet-rtps.c) exits packet scope. The RTPS dissector inserts wmem-allocated strings into pinfo->private_table, a GHashTable created with g_free as its key/value destructor. wmem memory must be freed through wmem's own scope system, not g_free. When wmem_leave_packet_scope() fires at the end of packet dissection and runs wmem_simple_free_all(), it frees all wmem-allocated memory in the packet pool. But the GHashTable destructor has already called g_free on those same pointers when the table is destroyed, producing a double-free on every string the RTPS dissector inserted. Fix removes the g_free destructor arguments from the hash table creation call.

